\name{cellucid_highlight_range}
\alias{cellucid_highlight_range}
\title{Highlight a range of values}
\usage{
cellucid_highlight_range(viewer, field, min, max, color, page)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{A continuous field or a gene, by name. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The field or gene name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{"obs" for a column of the cells, "var" for a gene. One of \code{"obs"}, \code{"var"}. Required.}}}
\item{min}{The smallest value included. A number. Required.}
\item{max}{The largest value included. A number. Required.}
\item{color}{The colour of the page the group goes on. With \code{page}, the colour of the page made (an existing page must already have it). Without, the page shown when it has this colour, else the first page that has it, else a new page of it. Text. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{page}{The page the group goes on, by name; a page of that name is made when there is none. Omitted: the page shown, or with \code{color}, a page of that colour. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Add the cells whose value of a continuous field or gene lies in a range, as the selected view shows them, as a group.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{highlight.range} (Highlights). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{highlights}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_highlight_range(viewer, field = list(key = "cell_type",
      source = "obs"), max = 0, min = 0)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
